  "verbalization": "Prednisolone is linked to Non-histaminic Angioedema through a chain of indications involving Triamcinolone. The evidence suggests that Prednisolone, through its indication for Chronic Primary Adrenal Insufficiency, Chondrocalcinosis, and Chronic Beryllium Disease, ultimately leads to Triamcinolone, which in turn is associated with Non-histaminic Angioedema. This pathway implies a potential mechanistic link where the use of Prednisolone may indirectly contribute to the development of Non-histaminic Angioedema via the administration of Triamcinolone. The shared use of Triamcinolone in multiple indications points to a possible overlapping pathophysiological mechanism, though the exact causal relationship remains unclear. The evidence supports a possible role of Triamcinolone in the pathogenesis of Non-histaminic Angioedema, but further investigation is needed to establish a definitive causal link.",
